## How to use these prompts

1. Open [Google AI Studio](https://aistudio.google.com/).
2. Start a project or open your existing project.
3. Paste the **Master Prompt** first.
4. Paste **Phase 1** and let AI Studio implement it.
5. Review the generated files and fix errors before proceeding.
6. Paste each subsequent phase prompt separately, from Phase 2 through Phase 10.
7. Keep a copy of the code after every completed phase, preferably in GitHub.
8. Never add real student records or payment credentials to prompts.

### Before moving to the next phase, use this review prompt

```text
Review the phase you just implemented.

Do not add new features yet.

1. Inspect all changed files and identify missing or incomplete functionality.
2. Check for compile errors, type errors, dependency problems, and broken imports.
3. Run available static analysis and automated tests.
4. Verify that Firebase authorization is enforced by backend logic and security rules, not only by the UI.
5. Check that all existing features from previous phases still work.
6. Fix issues that you can reproduce.
7. List any configuration or manual steps still required.
8. Report the actual test results and remaining limitations.

Do not claim a test passed unless it was actually run successfully.
```

**My recommendation:** Complete Phases 1–3 first and verify authentication, branch isolation, and security rules before entering real student information. These are foundational to every later feature, especially attendance, fees, and payments.